    "https://hr.hornet365.com/faculty-volunteer-early-retirement-incentive": {
      "title": "Faculty Volunteer Early Retirement Incentive",
      "description": "Faculty Volunteer Early Retirement Incentive PASSWORD HELP FACULTY + STAFF OPEN POSITIONS CLASSIFICATION AND COMPENSATION REMOTE WORK INSURANCE ENROLLMENT FACULTY VOLUNTEER EARLY RETIREMENT INCENTIVE Get in touch 555-555-5555 mymail@mailservice.com EMPORIA.EDU SEARCH STUDENTS EMPLOYEES FACULTY TECHSITE MARKETING + COMMUNICATION HUMAN RESOURCES FACULTY VOLUNTEER EARLY RETIREMENT INCENTIVE Faculty Volunteer Early Retirement Incentive This website intends to provide necessary information and resources related to the Faculty Voluntary Early Retirement Incentive (FVERI) announced by Emporia State University on April 18, 2025. As part of Emporia State University ongoing efforts to modernize and streamline our operations, we continue to build our annual budget following a zero-based budgeting model. This approach reflects our continued commitment to thoughtful, forward-looking planning to continually assess and adjust every aspect of our business for efficiency and prioritize the student experience. The FVERI timeline is summarized below. April 18, 2025 FVERI announced May 9, 2025 by 5 p.m. Deadline for Intent to Retire form to be submitted by employee Within 1 Business Day Employee shall receive confirmation of form and Separation Agreement (with signature block) via email May 12, 2025 by 5 p.m. Fully executed and completed Separation Agreement is due on May 12, 2025 to: humres@Emporia.edu. OR hand delivered to Human Resources April 18, 2025   to May 12, 2025 Includes mandatory 21-day review period Saturday, June 7, 2025 Date of separation (retirement) Friday, June 20, 2025* Estimated Payday for Receipt of Separation Payment (Separation Agreement must be and submitted to humres@Emporia.edu by 5 p.m., May 12, 2025) ﻿ *Program participants should be aware that it may take several weeks after the Retirement Date before the FVERI Incentive Payment processes. The date for payment is an estimated date based on the payroll calendar and estimated time for processing. Program participants will be notified of the exact date payment will be received once the Separation Agreement is executed. Program Guidelines Information Separation Agreement Official Program Guidelines FAQ Information on Working After Retirement Benefits Information Retirement Benefits Overview Additional Retirement Benefits Continuation of Health Care Benefits View Recent Hornet Announcements EMPORIA STATE UNIVERSITY 1 Kellogg Circle, Emporia, KS  66801 Questions? Please contact the IT Help Desk (620)341-5555 or helpdesk@emporia.edu Share by:"
    },
    "https://HORNET365.COM/FACULTY": {
      "title": "HUMAN RESOURCES AND PAYROLL",
      "description": "Faculty PASSWORD HELP STUDENTS EMPLOYEES FACULTY TECHSITE MARKETING + COMMUNICATION Get in touch 555-555-5555 mymail@mailservice.com EMPORIA.EDU SEARCH Home STUDENTS EMPLOYEES FACULTY TECHSITE MARKETING + COMMUNICATION Slide title Write your caption here Button Slide title Write your caption here Button Slide title Write your caption here Button Slide title Write your caption here Button FACULTY TOOLS Assignments Browse the Transfer Course Database Assessment: Submit Your Course-Level Report (SLOART) Course Schedule Detail Class List Grade Change Registration Overrides Grade Entry Week at a Glance Summer Pay Calculator Faculty Inclusive Teaching Resources ADVISOR TOOLS Advising Student Profile Browse the Transfer Course Database Course Schedule Registration History Student Week at a Glance Change of Registration (Add/Drop/Withdraw/Overload) Change of Undergraduate Student Curriculum (Major/Minor/Advisor/Catalog Changes) Degree Works Request for Graduate Credit Form Requirement Exception (Substitution or Exemption for Major/Minor/Concentration/Gen Ed Requirements or University Waiver) Student Academic Transcripts – Legacy ADVISING GLOSSARY Active Assignments– view instructor’s active courses for current term Assignment History– view instructor’s courses in past terms Course Schedule– view all courses offered for selected term Detail Class List– view instructor’s course assignments and detailed course roster Registration Overrides– allows instructor to submit registration overrides for specific student(s) Summary Class List– summary of course and roster Add/Drop Classes– make changes to student registration Advisee Grade Summary– view grades for advisee list Advisee Listing– view instructor’s advisee list Advisor-Look Up Classes– search all courses CRN Selection– view instructor’s course within a term Faculty Detail Schedule– view instructor’s schedule Week at a glance- view instructor’s weekly schedule by day and time Course Catalog– view all courses offered at ESU Syllabus Information– view syllabus information for instructor’s course assignments FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS – SSB9 Faculty and Advisors are now limited to view only their advisees and not the entire student population. This enhances our security to sensitive data per our security policy. Q – I can’t enter grades.  When I click on the student’s name nothing happens. A – To enter grades click on “Faculty Grade Entry” in Hornet 365 under Faculty & Advising.  Click on the course you want to add grades for.  If you have further questions contact the Office of the Registrar. Q – I can’t see all the students I used to be able to view. A – For security reasons, Faculty & Advisors are limited to only seeing information on their Advisees. Q – I need to see more students than just my Advisees. A – For security reasons some information will no longer be shared widely across campus.  Please contact the Office of the Registrar to review alternate methods of information retrieval. Q – What happened to the Concise Student Schedule? A – Concise Student Schedule is no longer available in the upgrade.  Advisors and students can find a summary of the class schedule on their Student Profile.  This information can also be found under Register for Classes by clicking on Schedule and Options or Schedule Details. Q – Do I always need to navigate back to Hornet 365 to perform a different task? A – No, once you navigate into Self Service Banner by selecting one of the tiles in Hornet 365, if you click on the “Emporia State University” logo at the top of the page you will be directed to your Faculty/Advising landing page.   You can select additional tasks from there. Q – How can I get to the various forms and tools available to faculty and advisors? A – Hornet 365 has Faculty Tools and Advisor Tools available under Faculty & Advisor.  Additionally you can also access these tools in Self Service Banner by clicking on the “Four Square” (located in the top left corner of the page, next to the Emporia State University Logo) HUMAN RESOURCES AND PAYROLL View Human Resources And Payroll MAPS AND CAMPUS View Maps And Campus FACULTY SENATE View Faculty Senate MOST USED SERVICES List of Services Canvas Canvas Internal Communication Portal Internal Communication Portal OneDrive OneDrive Outlook Outlook Panopto Panopto Zoom Zoom ALL FACULTY SERVICES Some pages may require VPN use when not on campus List of Services Antispam Antispam Banner 9 Admin Pages Banner 9 Admin Pages Bookstore Bookstore Bookstore for Faculty (AIP) Bookstore for Faculty (AIP) Bookings Bookings Campus Labs Campus Labs Campus Shared File Site Campus Shared File Site Canvas Canvas Cars Cars Cognos Cognos Conf + Sched Calendar Conf + Sched Calendar Corporate Engagement Corporate Engagement Degree Works Degree Works Downloads for Employees Downloads for Employees Emergency Alerts Emergency Alerts Faculty Qualifications Faculty Qualifications Faculty/Staff Directory Faculty/Staff Directory Form Central Form Central GoinGlobal GoinGlobal Google Apps Google Apps Heart of a Hornet Heart of a Hornet Hornet Announcements Hornet Announcements Hornet Central Hornet Central HornetLab (SkyLab) HornetLab (SkyLab) Hornet TV Hornet TV Internal Communication Portal Internal Communication Portal Internal Data Hub Internal Data Hub Library Connect Library Connect Microsoft Forms Microsoft Forms Microsoft Teams Microsoft Teams Navigate Navigate Newsstand Newsstand OnBase OnBase OneDrive OneDrive Outlook Outlook Panopto Panopto Parking Parking Pay Simulator Pay Simulator President Executive Orders FAQ President Executive Orders FAQ Records Retention Records Retention Rec Services Dashboard Rec Services Dashboard Sedona Sedona SharePoint SharePoint Strategic Plan Dashboard Strategic Plan Dashboard Student Concern Forms Student Concern Forms Update Your Info Update Your Info WebDAC Portal WebDAC Portal Zoom Zoom EMPORIA STATE UNIVERSITY 1 Kellogg Circle, Emporia, KS  66801 Questions? Please contact the IT Help Desk (620)341-5555 or helpdesk@emporia.edu Share by:"
